title: ch2_clean_first_hire
---
You clean four apartments a day and turn down three more. Your back has opinions about it. #line:ch2_clean_first_hire_01
Unpaid CEO: You can keep doing every job yourself, or you can start building a company. Pick one. #line:ch2_clean_first_hire_02
-> Write a job post and do it by the book. #line:ch2_clean_first_hire_03
    <<choose "hire">>
    Unpaid CEO: Payroll, insurance, a real contract. Now you're a boss with paperwork. #line:ch2_clean_first_hire_04
-> Keep it solo a while longer. #line:ch2_clean_first_hire_05
    <<choose "solo">>
    Unpaid CEO: Your knees will remind you of this conversation. #line:ch2_clean_first_hire_06
===

title: ch2_clean_vase
---
A crash from the living room. A client's vase lies in pieces. She says it cost four hundred dollars. #line:ch2_clean_vase_01
-> Apologize and pay for it. #line:ch2_clean_vase_02
    <<choose "pay">>
    She books you every week after that. You buy liability insurance the same day. #line:ch2_clean_vase_03
-> Ask for a receipt first. #line:ch2_clean_vase_04
    <<choose "doubt">>
    She finds a receipt for a hundred and fifty. She also finds another cleaner. #line:ch2_clean_vase_05
===

title: ch2_clean_office
---
A coworking space wants nightly cleaning on a twelve-month contract. Great money, paid net 30. #line:ch2_clean_office_01
You'd need someone working every night of the week. #line:ch2_clean_office_02
-> Sign it and staff the night shift. #line:ch2_clean_office_03
    <<choose "sign">>
    Steady revenue. Steady salaries, too, that leave before the client pays. #line:ch2_clean_office_04
-> Pass. Homes only for now. #line:ch2_clean_office_05
    <<choose "pass">>
    You keep your evenings. Someone else gets the contract. #line:ch2_clean_office_06
===

title: ch2_clean_cash
---
A new cleaner asks to be paid cash, off the books. Cheaper for both of us, she says. #line:ch2_clean_cash_01
-> Pay her on payroll like everyone else. #line:ch2_clean_cash_02
    <<choose "books">>
    It costs more. If she gets hurt on the job, she's covered. #line:ch2_clean_cash_03
-> Pay her cash. #line:ch2_clean_cash_04
    <<choose "cash">>
    You save a little every week and worry about it every night. #line:ch2_clean_cash_05
===

title: ch2_clean_green
---
Two clients ask whether you use non-toxic products. They have kids and a cat. #line:ch2_clean_green_01
-> Switch to green products and say so. #line:ch2_clean_green_02
    <<choose "switch">>
    Your flyer now says safe for kids and pets. The phone rings more. #line:ch2_clean_green_03
-> Stick with what cleans best. #line:ch2_clean_green_04
    <<choose "same">>
    Floors shine. One family quietly cancels. #line:ch2_clean_green_05
===

title: ch2_clean_referral
---
Half your new clients came from one building on Eastern Parkway. The doorman knows everyone. #line:ch2_clean_referral_01
-> Offer twenty-five dollars for every referral. #line:ch2_clean_referral_02
    <<choose "bonus">>
    Twenty-five dollars for a client who stays a year. Best ad you've ever bought. #line:ch2_clean_referral_03
-> Bring the doorman coffee and say thanks. #line:ch2_clean_referral_04
    <<choose "thanks">>
    He grins. Tony taught him the same trick years ago. #line:ch2_clean_referral_05
===
